{
    "background_story": "Zayden was a master perfumer with a nose that could detect even the subtlest scents. Growing up in a family of florists, he was surrounded by the sweet aromas of blooming flowers and the earthy smell of soil. As a child, he would spend hours in his parents' garden, sniffing and identifying the different fragrances. This early fascination led him to study perfumery in France, where he honed his skills and developed a unique talent for crafting scents that evoked emotions and memories. Zayden's perfumes became renowned for their complexity and depth, with clients seeking him out for bespoke fragrances that captured the essence of their favorite memories. His workshop was a treasure trove of scents, with rows of essential oils and rare extracts that he would blend with precision to create truly unforgettable aromas.",
